WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.837 --> 00:00:16.196
It was a busy day at Metro City Central Bank.

2
00:00:16.197 --> 00:00:20.048
"I need some money," a customer said.

3
00:00:20.049 --> 00:00:22.491
The bank teller typed on a computer.

4
00:00:22.492 --> 00:00:25.060
A drawer popped open.

5
00:00:25.061 --> 00:00:27.694
"Uh-oh," the bank teller said.

6
00:00:27.695 --> 00:00:30.686
"There's no more money in the drawer.

7
00:00:30.687 --> 00:00:34.631
Wait here. I'll get it from the safe."

8
00:00:34.632 --> 00:00:38.403
He went over to the safe, unlocked the door, and opened it.

9
00:00:38.404 --> 00:00:45.461
The bank teller gasped. "All the money is gone!"

10
00:00:45.462 --> 00:00:50.694
"Wow!" Mara said. "Saturn's rings are amazing."

11
00:00:50.695 --> 00:00:53.837
Roxy and her friends were in the computer center at school.

12
00:00:53.838 --> 00:00:56.715
They were doing research projects for science.

13
00:00:56.716 --> 00:01:00.917
"I'd like to run around Saturn on its rings," Jack said.

14
00:01:00.918 --> 00:01:06.281
Mara rolled her eyes. "You can't run on Saturn's rings, Jack.

15
00:01:06.282 --> 00:01:12.629
They're not solid. They're made of chunks of ice and rock that float around the planet."

16
00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:14.825
Terrell looked over from his computer.

17
00:01:14.826 --> 00:01:17.704
"I'm researching the first moon landing.

18
00:01:17.705 --> 00:01:20.313
You could definitely run on the moon.

19
00:01:20.314 --> 00:01:22.651
You'd need a spacesuit though."

20
00:01:22.652 --> 00:01:26.949
Roxy nodded. "Plus, there isn't much gravity on the moon.

21
00:01:26.950 --> 00:01:29.851
So you could jump really high."

22
00:01:29.852 --> 00:01:33.637
Jack stood up. "Earth, this is Astronaut Jack.

23
00:01:33.638 --> 00:01:35.767
I just landed on the moon.

24
00:01:35.768 --> 00:01:38.425
I'm going to try moon jumping now!"

25
00:01:38.426 --> 00:01:40.459
Jack jumped as high as he could.

26
00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:44.823
Roxy, Mara, and Terrell laughed.

27
00:01:44.824 --> 00:01:46.759
Miss Apricot walked over.

28
00:01:46.760 --> 00:01:51.429
"Jack, did you pick a topic for your project yet?"

29
00:01:51.430 --> 00:01:55.858
Jack scratched his head. "Uh, I might research aliens."

30
00:01:55.859 --> 00:01:57.730
Miss Apricot sighed.

31
00:01:57.731 --> 00:02:02.176
"Please pick something more serious than that.

32
00:02:02.177 --> 00:02:05.051
And stop jumping."

33
00:02:05.052 --> 00:02:08.463
"Okay, Miss Apricot." Jack sat back down.

34
00:02:08.464 --> 00:02:12.258
"What are you writing about, Roxy?" Terrell asked.

35
00:02:12.259 --> 00:02:16.133
"Well," Roxy said. "I picked the planet Mercury.

36
00:02:16.134 --> 00:02:18.567
But it's not very interesting."

37
00:02:18.568 --> 00:02:20.938
Terrell looked thoughtful for a moment.

38
00:02:20.939 --> 00:02:25.137
"I have an idea—Rocket Girl."

39
00:02:25.138 --> 00:02:28.905
Roxy tried not to laugh. She knew Terrell was kidding.

40
00:02:28.906 --> 00:02:30.828
"Very funny, Terrell.

41
00:02:30.829 --> 00:02:34.926
But Rocket Girl has more important things to do than help me."

42
00:02:34.927 --> 00:02:36.478
Terrell shook his head.

43
00:02:36.479 --> 00:02:40.169
"No, I meant you should write about Rocket Girl.

44
00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:42.497
She can fly through space, right?

45
00:02:42.498 --> 00:02:45.793
And she's probably as fast as a comet."

46
00:02:45.794 --> 00:02:50.711
Mara chuckled. "That's ridiculous, Terrell!"

47
00:02:50.712 --> 00:02:55.109
"It's even sillier than my alien idea!" Jack said.

48
00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:59.215
Just then Roxy's watch beeped.

49
00:02:59.216 --> 00:03:01.851
"I'll be right back," she whispered to Terrell.

50
00:03:01.852 --> 00:03:04.496
"Mayor Bloom is calling me."

51
00:03:04.497 --> 00:03:07.044
Roxy stepped out of the computer center.

52
00:03:07.045 --> 00:03:10.020
"Mayor Bloom, what's wrong?"

53
00:03:10.021 --> 00:03:13.423
"I need your help, Rocket Girl!" Mayor Bloom said.

54
00:03:13.424 --> 00:03:16.907
"Metro City Central Bank was just robbed."

55
00:03:16.908 --> 00:03:19.044
"Don't worry, Mayor," Roxy said.

56
00:03:19.045 --> 00:03:22.613
"I'll be there right away!"
